13. How to Make the $100 Credit Last

For the initial prototype:

* Use a cost-efficient model.
* Keep prompts concise.
* Avoid unnecessary agent-to-agent loops.
* Limit automatic retries.
* Start with 3–4 agents.
* Monitor Azure costs from the beginning.
* Add expensive tools only when necessary.
* Avoid having every agent respond to every message.

For example, don’t do:

ScrumMaster
   ↓
PM
   ↓
Developer
   ↓
QA
   ↓
Reviewer
   ↓
Documentation
   ↓
PM
   ↓
Developer
   ↓
QA
   ↓
...

without a termination condition.

Otherwise, an autonomous multi-agent loop can consume model credits very quickly.

